      "text": "TabbyAPI has no setting for draft_confidence, the -dc of chat.py. Without it the Generator's dynamic drafting targets 0.4 instead of the recipe's 0.6. A two-line patch to TabbyAPI (common/config_models.py adds draft_model.draft_confidence, backends/exllamav3/model.py passes it to the Generator) makes the value configurable; that is the only change to TabbyAPI."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "EXL3_NGRAM_STREAM=0 comes from the recipe launcher and holds the 32.6 GB n-gram (PLE) table in system RAM instead of the engine default of streaming its rows from disk per forward. The recipe README says elsewhere that the RAM table measured no faster with MTP; the launcher sets it anyway, and it is followed here as written. It is why the server process holds about 36 GB of host memory on top of the device weights."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "On GB10 page cache counts against memory the CUDA allocator can use, and exllamav3 sizes its load against cudaMemGetInfo, which reports MemFree rather than MemAvailable. After the 85 GB download and a sha256 pass the page cache held about 84 GB; the recipe's drop-model-cache.sh (posix_fadvise DONTNEED on every pack file) runs before each load."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "The model writes tool calls in Qwen's XML form (<function=name><parameter=key>value</parameter></function>), so TabbyAPI needs tool_format qwen3_coder; tool calls then come back as OpenAI tool_calls with finish_reason tool_calls, and thinking lands in reasoning_content with reasoning true."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "From a Mac on the same LAN, requests to dgx.local took about 4 s longer than the server's own timing because of mDNS name resolution; the harness ran on the box against 127.0.0.1, so none of that is in these rows."
    }
